  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Kpmg recorded $329M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Kpmg won 135 awards so far, with an average award size of $2.4M, and obligations are down 21.9% year over year. Kpmg obligations moved from $411M in FY21 to $429M in FY22, $451M in FY23 and $492M in FY24, then shifted to $421M in FY25 and to $329M in FY26. Kpmg work is concentrated with a few large federal buyers: the Department of Defense obligated $171M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $67.5M in FY2026 to date. Kpmg delivers accounting and advisory services at scale: Offices of Certified Public Accountants account for $251M and Other Accounting Services account for $40.7M. Kpmg also records meaningful totals in Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $23.7M and Other Computer Related Services at $12.2M. Kpmg shows smaller FY2026 to date totals across several additional NAICS lines listed in the market roster.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have Kpmg obligations moved over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Kpmg obligations rose from $411M in FY21 to $492M in FY24, then moved to $421M in FY25 and to $329M in FY26. Kpmg obligations are down 21.9% year over year in FY2026 to date. Kpmg recorded 135 awards in FY2026 to date, with an average award size of $2.4M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Kpmg's largest federal customers and what markets do they fund?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is Kpmg's largest buyer at $171M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services at $67.5M and the Department of Energy at $17.7M. Offices of Certified Public Accountants is Kpmg's largest market at $251M, with Other Accounting Services at $40.7M and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $23.7M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Kpmg make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Kpmg has $329M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Kpmg won 135 awards in FY2026 to date with an average award size of $2.4M. Kpmg obligations are down 21.9% year over year. Kpmg obligations followed a trend from $411M in FY21 up to $492M in FY24 and then to $421M in FY25 before reaching $329M in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Kpmg?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is Kpmg's largest federal customer at $171M. Other significant buyers include the Department of Health and Human Services at $67.5M, the Department of Energy at $17.7M, the Department of Veterans Affairs at $13.8M, and the Department of Justice at $10.7M. Additional buyers listed for FY2026 to date include the General Services Administration at $9.2M and the Department of the Interior at $8.8M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Kpmg sell to the government?",
